module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.SerreSubcategoryModel
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.PerfectGeneratorInduction

/-!
# The perfect generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` at an arbitrary model of the derived category

`HasDerivedCategory.{w} C` carries a *chosen* localization of `CochainComplex C ℤ` as data, so
`D(𝒪_X)` is a different category for each choice and a statement proved at one says nothing about
another until it is transported. [Stacks, Tag 09IS] is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedQCoh/PerfectGeneratorInduction.lean` at the locally small
model `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory`, and the implementation notes there
explain that this is forced: the affine base case runs through the derived Spec–Γ equivalence of
[Stacks, Tag 06Z0] and the quasi-coherence of `Rj_*`, both of which are available at that model and
at no other. That is a constraint on the *proof*; the conclusion is a statement about whichever
`D(𝒪_X)` is in force, and this file carries it to all of them.

The transport is the comparison equivalence `StacksDraft.DerivedModel.modelEquiv` of two chosen
models, with its three already-available compatibilities: it identifies the two localizations out
of cochain complexes, so perfectness is carried by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isPerfect_modelEquiv_iff`; it identifies the two cohomology functors,
so membership in `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is carried by
`StacksDraft.DerivedModel.derivedCategoryB_modelEquiv_functor_obj_iff`; and it commutes with the
shift by `StacksDraft.Perfect.derivedEquivalenceCommShift`, so
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful` carries the vanishing of the
morphisms out of all shifts of the generator.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_anyModel` — for a
  quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme `X` and *any* chosen `D(𝒪_X)`, the subcategory
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is weakly generated by a single object which is perfect in `D(𝒪_X)`.

## Implementation notes

*Why the conclusion is spelled over `SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf`.* `X.Modules` and
`SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf` are definitionally equal but carry separately declared
`Category`, `Preadditive` and `Abelian` instances, and the instance that makes `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` a
shift-stable subcategory —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentDerived.isTriangulated_derivedQuasicoherent` — is stated in
the second spelling. Since `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` asks for a
`CategoryTheory.HasShift` on the full subcategory, the statement below only typechecks in that
spelling; in the first one the instance is not found at a model other than the global one.

*Why the model is an instance binder and not an explicit argument.* The prerequisites of
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` on the full subcategory —
`CategoryTheory.HasShift`, and behind it `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderShift` and the
additivity of the shift functors — are all found by instance search from a *seated*
`HasDerivedCategory`. An explicitly given model is not seated, and the statement then fails to
elaborate. This is the opposite of the discipline urged by
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/ModelComparisonTransport.lean`, and it is why the two models
appearing inside the proof are named explicitly even though the one in the statement is not.

*No `@[stacks]` attribute.* The tag is carried where the theorem is proved, by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs` and
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isZero_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero`. What is added here is
the independence of the chosen localization, which is an artefact of formalizing the derived
category as a chosen localization with a chosen morphism universe and about which the source has
nothing to say; this follows the convention of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/ModelComparisonTransport.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 079Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079Q)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open StacksDraft.DerivedModel

universe u w

namespace Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 09IS] at an arbitrary model, in the ambient derived category.** Let `X` be a
quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme and let a model of `D(𝒪_X)` be chosen. There is an object `P`
of `D(𝒪_X)` which lies in `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`, is perfect, and detects the zero object of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`: an object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is zero exactly when every morphism `P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E` vanishes.

This is `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs`, read in the ambient category by
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff` and transported along
the comparison equivalence of the locally small model with the given one. The generator goes over
to `P`; perfectness is carried by `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isPerfect_modelEquiv_iff` and
membership in `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` by
`StacksDraft.DerivedModel.derivedCategoryB_modelEquiv_functor_obj_iff`. Detection travels because
the comparison is fully faithful and commutes with the shift: an object `N` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` at the
given model receiving only zero maps from the shifts of `P` is the image of
`e⁻¹N`, which receives only zero maps from the shifts of the original generator
(`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful`) and is therefore zero.

This is the ambient-category step of
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_anyModel`; it is stated
over `X.Modules`, the spelling in which the two models can be compared, rather than over
`SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf`. -/
private theorem exists_isPerfect_detecting_isZero_anyModel (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] [h : HasDerivedCategory.{w} X.Modules] :
    ∃ P : DerivedCategory X.Modules,
      DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := X.Modules)
          (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) P ∧
        @Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect X.toRingedSpace h P ∧
          ∀ E : DerivedCategory X.Modules, DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := X.Modules)
            (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) E →
              (IsZero E ↔ ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E), g = 0) := by
  have hB := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre.isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre X
  obtain ⟨E, hEperf, hEgen⟩ := hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs X
  rw [ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff] at hEgen
  let e := modelEquiv (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory X) h
  let : e.functor.CommShift ℤ := StacksDraft.Perfect.derivedEquivalenceCommShift _ h
  let : e.functor.PreservesZeroMorphisms :=
    Functor.preservesZeroMorphisms_of_isLeftAdjoint _
  have hcui : (@DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB X.Modules _ _ h
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf)).IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms :=
    DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB_isClosedUnderIsomorphisms _ hB
  refine ⟨e.functor.obj E.obj,
    (derivedCategoryB_modelEquiv_functor_obj_iff
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) _ h E.obj).2 E.2,
    (isPerfect_modelEquiv_iff (X := X.toRingedSpace) _ h E.obj).1 hEperf,
    fun N hN => ⟨fun hz n g => hz.eq_of_tgt _ _, fun hzero => ?_⟩⟩
  refine (Functor.map_isZero e.functor ?_).of_iso (e.counitIso.app N).symm
  refine hEgen (e.inverse.obj N) ?_ (fun n g => forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful
    e.functor (e.counitIso.app N) hzero n g)
  refine (derivedCategoryB_modelEquiv_functor_obj_iff
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) _ h _).1 ?_
  exact hcui.of_iso (e.counitIso.app N).symm hN

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 09IS] at an arbitrary model of `D(𝒪_X)`.** Let `X` be a quasi-compact
quasi-separated scheme and let a model of the derived category of `𝒪_X`-modules be chosen. Then
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` has a weak triangulated generator which is perfect as an object of `D(𝒪_X)`.

For the locally small model of `StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean` this is
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs`, which is where the theorem is proved
and where the tag is carried; taking the model to be
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard X.Modules` gives the statement in the form the
standard-model files of the repository can consume.

The proof reads `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs` in the ambient derived
category, transports it (the private step above), and reads the result back inside `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`;
both readings are
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff`. -/
theorem exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_anyModel (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    [h : HasDerivedCategory.{w} (SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf)] :
    ∃ E : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB
        (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf)).FullSubcategory,
      @Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect X.toRingedSpace h E.obj ∧
        (ObjectProperty.singleton E).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator := by
  obtain ⟨P, hmem, hPperf, hPdet⟩ := exists_isPerfect_detecting_isZero_anyModel X (h := h)
  refine ⟨⟨P, hmem⟩, hPperf, ?_⟩
  rw [ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff]
  exact fun M hM hzero => (hPdet M hM).2 hzero

end Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel

end
